00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:11,600
And once these are found in terms of issues, Jenkins will automatically fail the build and stop it from being deployed.

341
00:30:11,600 --> 00:30:15,600
So again, the choices are based on our metrics that we looked at from the reporting earlier.

342
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:21,600
Same with the confidence level. We can actually permit a certain number of issues if we want to, you know, a threshold.

343
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:25,600
We can also generate a scan report as a result of this.

344
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:29,600
So from a developer's perspective, who are typically going to be doing the pipeline jobs,

345
00:30:29,600 --> 00:30:31,600
they actually don't even need access to the UI.

346
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:37,600
They can initiate the scan from the pipeline and generate a copy of that report stored where they wish,

347
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:41,600
and then analyze those results as well.

348
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:47,600
Once we save that, we can go ahead and build and that's going to essentially create an API generated scan against Enterprise.

